Repository gates

Usage: xtask <COMMAND>

Commands:
  devgates          The seam ratchet (ADR 0001): production code against `xtask/seam_allowlist.txt`
  lints             Lossy Rust shapes this repository does not write
  deps              Dependency direction between the workspace crates
  fixtures          Conventions of the independent fixture projects under fixtures/
  release-check     Version consistency between the workspace and the release manifest
  milestones        Every milestone named in the documentation resolves to one roadmap row
  adrs              Every decision record has one number, carries it in its heading, is listed once
                    in the book under it, and is named only as it is
  invariants        Every critical decision has a row saying what holds it at every layer, each
                    naming what the tree defines, and every hole is one somebody owns
  ratchets          Everything that may shrink and never grow, held to where this change meets
                    `origin/main`
  surfaces          Every crate declares what its visibility means; incidental APIs are compiled
                    privately
  reached           Every public function of an incidental surface is reached by something that
                    ships
  waivers           A second opinion, by body shape alone, on every catch-all the ledger waives
  tracked           Nothing a build writes is committed: no tracked path lies under a directory
                    named `target`
  skipped           Every skipped target in the mutation configuration is a target Cargo declares
  claims            Every claim of `.rust-mutants.toml` names as many mutations as it says, asked of
                    the engine's own locator
  fuzz-clippy       Clippy every independent fuzz target under the root workspace lint policy
  docflows          Every workflow the documentation shows passes actionlint against this
                    repository's own actions
  receipt           Run the engine over a package, sealed, and write the receipt of one module's
                    mutants for a registry decision (docs/invariants.md)
  kani-laws         Prove every production law with Kani, or read back the proof of exactly these
                    inputs, and audit it either way
  kani-laws-audit   Fail closed unless Kani's raw law export proves every assertion reachable and
                    every cover satisfiable
  wasi-testsuite    Run every preview1 test of WebAssembly/wasi-testsuite on the sealed host as a
                    sealed test instance runs, and fail unless each ends as
                    crates/rust-mutants/tests/wasi-testsuite.toml says
  proofaudit        Whether a completed run's verdicts are the ones its own recording supports (ADR
                    0004)
  engine-audit      Whether a completed engine run's report is the one its own rows, recording, and
                    ledger support (ADR 0004)
  report-diff       What changed between two stored assurance reports
  sbom              What a release is made of, as a `CycloneDX` document
  bundle            The release archive of one target, holding every shipped binary where `cargo
                    binstall` reads it, and its SHA-256
  coverage-ratchet  Enforce the region-coverage floors recorded in this tree
  remote-check      The whole suite of this commit on the other machines, before it is pushed
  all               Every repository-tree gate, in order
  slot              Runs a command once this machine's lane for it is free, and holds the lane until
                    the command ends
  pre-push          The pre-push hook: the exact commit being pushed, checked in this repository's
                    one reusable tree
  tidy              Runs a command with a temporary directory of its own, and fails naming whatever
                    the command left in it (ADR 0006)
  help              Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help
